Subject : [NCI] Attn to control the heavy cargoes and not make big shortfall.

TO : All loading offices
CC  : CCE, ASI
FM : CTY - AE

Above all things, thank you for your hard efforts and cooperation.
We fully recognized well that the sales activity isn't easy under these tough situation
and especially collecting cargoes with high CMPB but light cargoes.

However, since from increase of BSA on NCI, the weight issue has been serious more than before.
The table below is the load/weight status from WK42 ~ 46.
As we repeatedly emphasized, the base ton of NCI is 12 ton,
however most of loading offices have the weight issue as highligthed in red !!
[cid:3220.jpg@12345678.87654321]
The figures above is just average, it can be alluded that there were some cargoes over 20 ton per TEU even.
Because the BSA has been increased, just collecting of cargoes with heavy weight can't be solution.
If loading the heavy cargoes, we can't use the space economically due to the limited BWA and
may miss an opportunity for getting the profitable cargoes with light weight.

So, all offices are advised to refer to the basic but important guideline below.
- Please get into close more with the customer to have high CMPB with light weight
  by referring to the average CMPB status above.
- QTA doesn't mean a guaranteed space.
- The more you get heavy cargoes(WGT), the less you get space(TEU)
- The control for weight cargoes should be attended in advance.
- In these days, some offices has made the big shortfall which can't be accepted.
  Thoroughly check the f'cast often and enhance its accuracy.


Your keen attention for the guide and sincere coooperation would be appreciated and
can take the advantage for getting space and achieving your KPI.



Tks & B.rgds



